<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulrich I, Count of East Frisia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1408–<a href="/years/1466">1466</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Ulrich Cirksena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulrich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-cirksena">Cirksena</a> was a Frisian chieftain who, after a century of feuds among the chiefs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-frisia">East Frisia</a>, brought most of the region under his rule. In 1464 Emperor Frederick III made him an imperial count, founding the County of East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a> and the Cirksena dynasty, which ruled it until 1744.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulrich-i-count-of-east-frisia.jpg" alt="Ulrich I, Count of East Frisia" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Not mentioned · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulrich_I_(Ostfriesischen_Landschaft).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
